# hooks/run-hook.cmd is a polyglot: valid as both a POSIX shell script and a
# Windows batch file. Its bash path relies on a heredoc terminator
# (`CMDBLOCK`) matching a line literally -- a CRLF line ending (e.g. from a
# clone with core.autocrlf=true) makes the terminator fail to match, which
# silently swallows the rest of the file into the heredoc instead of raising
# a visible error. Force LF regardless of clone-time autocrlf settings.
hooks/run-hook.cmd text eol=lf
hooks/session-start text eol=lf
commands/*.md text eol=lf
